+
+#### [Juriscraper](https://github.com/freelawproject/juriscraper)
+> **Description:** Juriscraper is a production-grade scraper library for American court websites. Its README explains that it gathers judicial opinions, oral arguments, and PACER data, and that it is intentionally extensible for new geographies, media types, and court sources. This makes it valuable for lawyers, litigation support teams, and legal data engineers who need reliable collection pipelines before AI summarization or analytics can even begin. **GitHub metadata:** last commit/activity date `2026-03-27`, `497` stars, primary language `HTML`, license `BSD-2-Clause`.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/freelawproject/juriscraper](https://github.com/freelawproject/juriscraper)
+- **Stars:** 497 ⭐
+- **Language:** HTML
