+# Best AI Tools for Lawyers 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-lawyers-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best AI tools for lawyers 2026 starts with one constraint: every project in this list must be a public GitHub repository, not a proprietary SaaS pitch. This collection focuses on open source legal research, contract analysis, document automation, privacy, e-signing, and legal NLP projects that lawyers, law firms, legal ops teams, and legal engineers can actually inspect, fork, and self-host.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `CourtListener`, `Juriscraper`, and `Korean Law MCP` are the strongest open repositories here for legal research and primary-law access.
+- `OpenContracts`, `LexNLP`, and `ContextGem` are the most practical contract-review and extraction building blocks.
+- `docassemble`, `AssemblyLine`, and `Open Agreements` are the best open source choices for guided legal workflows and document generation.
+- `DocuSeal` is the strongest GitHub-native open source e-signing option in this list.
+- This repo stays strict: GitHub URLs only, no closed SaaS products, and gaps are called out instead of padded.
+
+## Why This List
+Most “AI tools for lawyers” lists are dominated by closed vendors, thin wrappers, and products that cannot be audited for privacy, accuracy, or data handling. For legal work, that is a bad default. Open source matters because lawyers need inspectable workflows, self-hosting options, repeatable citations, and the ability to validate how search, extraction, redaction, and document automation actually behave.
+
+This list broadens the search beyond “lawyer chatbot” repos because the best AI tools for lawyers 2026 are often infrastructure: legal research engines, citation parsers, contract analytics frameworks, document assembly platforms, and privacy/compliance tooling that can be combined into a real legal stack.
+
+## Open Source Tools
